aining performance.', 'A smaller student model designed to learn from a larger teacher BERT model, aiming for faster inference and reduced size.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2, 3]}, 'BERT': {'type': ['method', 'method', 'generic', 'generic'], 'description': ['A large Transformer-based language model used as the teacher model in knowledge distillation to train TinyBERT.', 'A large Transformer-based language model used as the teacher model in the knowledge distillation process to transfer knowledge to TinyBERT.', 'A large Transformer-based language model used as a teacher to transfer knowledge to the smaller TinyBERT model.', 'A large Transformer-based language model used as a teacher to transfer knowledge to the TinyBERT student model.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2, 3]}, 'GLUE benchmark': {'type': ['dataset', 'DATASET', 'dataset', 'dataset'], 'description': ['A benchmark used to evaluate the performance of language models on various natural language processing tasks.', 'A collection of diverse natural language understanding tasks used to evaluate the performance of TinyBERT and compare it against other models.', 'A collection of natural language understanding tasks used to evaluate the performance of language models, including tasks like CoLA, MNLI, and MRPC.', 'A collection of natural language understanding tasks used to evaluate the performance of language models, including tasks like MNLI, MRPC, and CoLA.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2, 3]}, 'Two-stage learning framework': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A learning approach for TinyBERT that includes general distillation (pre-training) and task-specific distillation (fine-tuning).'], 'source_chunk_index': [0]}, 'DistilBERT': {'type': ['method', 'method', 'generic', 'method'], 'description': ['A baseline model used for comparison with TinyBERT.', 'A knowledge distillation method used as a baseline for comparison with TinyBERT. It is a distilled version of BERT, designed to be smaller and faster while maintaining performance.', 'Another baseline model used for comparison with TinyBERT, known for its efficiency in terms of model size and inference speed.', 'The DistilBERT learning strategy is re-implemented and trained following the implementation procedure described in their papers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2, 2]}, 'BERT-PKD': {'type': ['method', 'method', 'generic', 'method'], 'description': ['A baseline model used for comparison with TinyBERT.', 'A knowledge distillation method used as a baseline for comparison with TinyBERT. It is a variant of BERT that uses knowledge distillation.', 'A baseline model used for comparison with TinyBERT, employing a similar knowledge distillation approach.', 'The BERT-PKD learning strategy is re-implemented and trained following the implementation procedure described in their papers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2, 2]}, 'Embedding layer': {'type': ['generic', 'method', 'method'], 'description': ['A layer in the BERT model from which knowledge is distilled to TinyBERT.', 'The output of the embedding layer, used as a component in the Transformer distillation method to fit different representations from BERT layers.', 'The initial layer in the BERT model that transforms input tokens into vector representations. Knowledge is distilled from this layer in the proposed Transformer distillation method.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 0, 0]}, 'Hidden states': {'type': ['generic', 'method', 'method'], 'description': ["Internal representations of the BERT model's layers, used in the Transformer distillation process.", 'The hidden states derived from the Transformer layer, used as a component in the Transformer distillation method to fit different representations from BERT layers.', 'The internal representations of the input at each layer of the BERT model. Knowledge is distilled from the hidden states of the Transformer layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 0, 0]}, 'Prediction layer logits': {'type': ['generic', 'method'], 'description': ['The output of the prediction layer in BERT, used in the Transformer distillation process.', "The output of the prediction layer in BERT, which represents the model's predictions. Knowledge is distilled from these logits."], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 0]}, 'Pre-training': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The initial stage of the two-stage learning framework, where TinyBERT is trained on a large corpus.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0]}, 'Fine-tuning': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The second stage of the two-stage learning framework, where TinyBERT is trained on task-specific data.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0]}, 'Wikipedia': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['A large-scale unsupervised text corpus used for pre-training TinyBERT in the general distillation stage.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0]}, 'Logits': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The logits output by the prediction layer, used as a component in the Transformer distillation method to fit different representations from BERT layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [0]}, 'Head Attention (MHA)': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['A component of the Transformer layer that calculates a weighted sum of values, with weights computed by applying a softmax operation on the attention matrix A.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Embedding-layer distillation': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A distillation technique that focuses on transferring knowledge from the embedding layer of the teacher BERT model to the student TinyBERT model.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'GLUE': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['A benchmark for evaluating the performance of natural language understanding systems, consisting of a collection of diverse natural language understanding tasks.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Feed-Forward Network (FFN)': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A fully connected feed-forward network within the Transformer layer, consisting of two linear transformations and a ReLU activation function. Its output, or intermediate representations, can be used in Transformer distillation.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'GloVe word embeddings': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['Word embeddings from the GloVe model, used in conjunction with a pre-trained language model BERT for word-level replacement during data augmentation in the task-specific distillation stage.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Loss Functions (Equations 7, 8, 9, and 10)': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ["The specific mathematical formulations used to quantify the difference between the teacher and student models' outputs during the distillation process. These equations define the objectives that TinyBERT aims to optimize to learn from BERT."], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Layer Mapping Function': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The function, g(m) = 3 × m, that determines which layers of the teacher BERT model are used to train the student TinyBERT model. In this case, TinyBERT learns from every 3 layers of BERT BASE.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'English Wikipedia': {'type': ['DATASET'], 'description': ['A large text corpus used in the general distillation stage to pre-train TinyBERT.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'CoLA': {'type': ['task', 'dataset'], 'description': ["The Corpus of Linguistic Acceptability, a task within the GLUE benchmark that assesses a model's ability to predict linguistic acceptability judgments.", 'A part of the GLUE benchmark, used to evaluate the performance of language models.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3]}, 'MNLI': {'type': ['task', 'dataset', 'task'], 'description': ['The Multi-Genre Natural Language Inference task, a part of the GLUE benchmark used to evaluate natural language understanding models.', 'A part of the GLUE benchmark, used to evaluate the performance of language models.', "A natural language inference task from the GLUE benchmark, used to evaluate TinyBERT's performance."], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3, 3]}, 'MRPC': {'type': ['task', 'dataset'], 'description': ['The Microsoft Research Paraphrase Corpus, a GLUE benchmark task focused on paraphrase identification.', 'A part of the GLUE benchmark, used to evaluate the performance of language models.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3]}, 'Intermediate Layer Distillation': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A distillation method used in TinyBERT where knowledge is transferred from the teacher model to the student model at the intermediate layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'QQP': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['A dataset used for evaluating TinyBERT, specifically for tasks related to question-pair similarity.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'QNLI': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['A dataset used for evaluating TinyBERT, specifically for question answering and natural language inference tasks.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'BERT-PKD Learning Strategy': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The specific learning strategy used for BERT-PKD, including details on the number of layers, training epochs, batch size, and learning rate, as described in the original BERT-PKD paper.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'DistilBERT Learning Strategy': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The specific learning strategy used for DistilBERT, including details on the number of layers, training epochs, batch size, and learning rate, as described in the original DistilBERT paper.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'BERT SMALL Learning Strategy': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The specific learning strategy used for BERT SMALL, including details on the number of layers, training epochs, batch size, and learning rate, as described in the original BERT work.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'BERT SMALL': {'type': ['method', 'generic'], 'description': ['The learning strategy for BERT SMALL strictly follows the same learning strategy as described in the original BERT work (Devlin et al. 2018).', 'A smaller version of BERT, used as a baseline and compared with TinyBERT.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3]}, 'SQuAD v1.1 and v2.0': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['Question answering datasets used to evaluate the effectiveness of TinyBERT.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'Stanford Sentiment Treebank': {'type': ['dataset', 'task'], 'description': ['A binary single-sentence classification task where the goal is to predict the sentiment of movie reviews.', 'A binary single-sentence classification task where the goal is to predict the sentiment of movie reviews, used to evaluate TinyBERT.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 3]}, 'SQuAD v1.1': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ["A question answering task, used to evaluate TinyBERT's performance."], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'SQuAD v2.0': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ["A question answering task, used to evaluate TinyBERT's performance."], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'Data augmentation': {'description': ['A technique used to increase the diversity of training data, particularly in the task-specific distillation stage, to improve model performance.', 'A method used to increase the size and diversity of the training data, particularly in the task-specific distillation stage, to improve the performance of TinyBERT.', 'The process of artificially increasing the amount of training data by creating modified versions of existing data, used in the task-specific distillation stage.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2]}, 'Attention matrices': {'description': ['Matrices representing the attention weights in the Transformer layers, used in the Transformer distillation process.', 'The attention matrices derived from the Transformer layer, used as a component in the Transformer distillation method to fit different representations from BERT layers.', 'The matrices that represent the attention weights learned by the Transformer layers in BERT. Knowledge is distilled from these matrices to capture linguistic knowledge.', 'A component of the BERT model used in the Transformer distillation process, specifically as a fitting target to transfer linguistic knowledge from the teacher to the student model.'], 'type': ['method', 'generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1]}, 'Loss Functions': {'description': ['Several loss functions are designed to fit different representations from BERT layers, including the embedding layer output, hidden states and attention matrices from the Transformer layer, and the logits output by the prediction layer.', "The mathematical functions used to quantify the difference between the teacher and student model's outputs, guiding the knowledge transfer process in Transformer distillation. Several loss functions are designed to fit different representations from BERT layers."], 'type': ['method', 'GENERIC'], 'source_chunk_index': [0]}, 'General distillation': {'description': ['The first stage of the two-stage learning framework, using a large corpus to initialize TinyBERT and help it learn rich knowledge from the teacher BERT.', 'The pre-training stage of the two-stage TinyBERT learning framework, using a large corpus like Wikipedia to initialize the student model.', 'A pre-training stage where TinyBERT learns knowledge from intermediate layers of the teacher BERT model.'], 'type': ['method', 'generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 2, 3]}, 'Task-specific distillation': {'description': ["The second stage of the two-stage learning framework, which re-performs Transformer distillation on an augmented task-specific dataset to further improve TinyBERT's performance.", 'A fine-tuning stage where TinyBERT continues learning task-specific knowledge from a fine-tuned teacher BERT model.', 'The fine-tuning stage of the two-stage TinyBERT learning framework, leveraging data augmentation and a fine-tuned BERT teacher.'], 'type': ['method', 'generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 2, 3]}, 'Prediction-layer distillation': {'description': ['A distillation technique that focuses on transferring knowledge from the prediction layer of the teacher BERT model to the student TinyBERT model.', 'A distillation method used in TinyBERT where knowledge is transferred from the teacher model to the student model at the prediction layer.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 2]}}
